# Kanban (new)

Purpose: instances as cards in columns keyed by an enum field, drag
to update. Exists because for flow-shaped work (pipelines, hiring)
the column IS the status; dragging a card is the fastest field-edit
in the product.

Size/position: drag + resize on the canvas (dnd), never in the menu.
Relevancy: 🔥 core · ⭐ valuable · 💤 later

| Option | Category | Relevancy | Values / default | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| title | display | 🔥 | text | |
| groupBy | data | 🔥 | enum field | columns = enum values |
| card fields | display | 🔥 | field[] (default name + 2) | card body lines |
| drag to update | display | 🔥 | on / off | off = read-only board |
| concept | filter | 🔥 | conceptId | |
| conditions | filter | 🔥 | SidebarCondition[] | |
| match | filter | 🔥 | all / any | |
| visible columns | display | ⭐ | all / subset, ordered | hide "lost", reorder |
| empty columns | display | ⭐ | show / hide | |
| card order | display | ⭐ | manual / orderBy field | within column |
| archived | filter | ⭐ | exclude (default) / include | |
| column width | layout | 💤 | auto / fixed | horizontal scroll past fit |
| icon | display | 💤 | icon name / none | |
| column counts | display | 💤 | on / off | header badges |
| wip limit | display | 💤 | off / n per column | over-limit tint |
